{
  "what": "The data a click on a reminder notification carries (DESIGN §14.3). The phone's scheduler writes it with reminderTapData (shared/reminderTap.ts) into each notification; the desktop's reminder worker writes it with host_core::reminders::Trigger::tap_data into the toast it shows. Both apps read it back with reminderTapOf.",
  "why": "Two languages write the same keys, and nothing ties them together but this file. A key spelt differently in Rust would make every desktop toast click open nothing, silently, and only on a real Windows machine with a reminder ringing.",
  "readBy": [
    "crates/host-core/src/reminders.rs (tests::tap_contract)",
    "src/intl/reminderTap.contract.test.ts"
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "an occurrence of an own series",
      "source": {
        "item_id": "series-1",
        "item_kind": "event",
        "container_id": "work",
        "start": "2026-11-16T09:00:00+00:00",
        "title": "Standup"
      },
      "data": {
        "itemId": "series-1",
        "itemKind": "event",
        "containerId": "work",
        "start": "2026-11-16T09:00:00+00:00",
        "title": "Standup"
      },
      "tap": {
        "kind": "event",
        "eventId": "series-1",
        "calendarId": "work",
        "start": "2026-11-16T09:00:00+00:00",
        "title": "Standup"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a single change of a series, by its own id",
